---
import LegalPage from "../components/LegalPage.astro";
import { GITHUB_REPOSITORY_URL } from "../lib/site";
const sections = [["scope", "Scope"], ["data", "Your data and connections"], ["third-parties", "Third parties"]] as const;
---
<LegalPage title="Privacy information — Weavra" description="Privacy information for the Weavra development project." heading="Privacy information" lede="Weavra is a development project. This page explains its current scope; it is not the privacy policy of an inherited hosted service." sections={sections}>
  <section id="scope">
    <p class="section-number">01</p><h2>Scope</h2>
    <p>This distribution does not offer a Weavra-hosted account, relay or cloud service. The original T3 Tools policies describe a separate operator and are not adopted as Weavra policies.</p>
    <p>See the <a href={GITHUB_REPOSITORY_URL}>source repository</a> for the implementation and configuration applicable to your build. Historical attribution remains in the repository notices and component licenses.</p>
  </section>
  <section id="data">
    <p class="section-number">02</p><h2>Your data and connections</h2>
    <p>Sessions, settings and credentials may be stored on your device or in environments you control. When you connect a provider or remote environment, prompts, files and related content can be transmitted to that destination. Review your configuration before using confidential information.</p>
    <p>Protect local data, backups and credentials. Manage provider-held information directly with the provider. This page does not promise deletion of information held by another operator.</p>
  </section>
  <section id="third-parties">
    <p class="section-number">03</p><h2>Third parties</h2>
    <p>Providers, integrations, repository hosting and any operator hosting a copy of this website have their own data practices. Following an external link or enabling a network integration is not a guarantee of offline operation.</p>
    <p>No T3 Tools privacy address is presented as a Weavra contact, and no new retention, jurisdiction or service-operator commitments are made here.</p>
  </section>
</LegalPage>
